{"id": 23, "ts": 1780622151.8829918, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I remain inclined to keep Candidate\u202fA as the provisional lead, but I\u2019m now more concerned about the missing evidence on stress resilience and crew cooperation\u2014both critical for long\u2011distance flights. While A\u2019s technical strengths (anticipating danger, complex\u2011connection insight, spatial vision, strong leadership) are compelling, we have no data confirming they stay calm under pressure or work constructively with a crew. By contrast, Candidate\u202fC does have documented decision\u2011quality under pressure (\u201ccan make correct decisions quickly\u201d and \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d) and creates a positive crew atmosphere, albeit with communication and egocentricity concerns. This makes C a stronger alternative on the two most uncertain criteria for A. Unless we can uncover evidence that A also performs well under stress and cooperates effectively, I\u2019m leaning toward Candidate\u202fC as the next best option."}
