{"id": 28, "ts": 1780622213.3223581, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s focus on the missing stress\u2011resilience and crew\u2011cooperation data for Candidate\u202fA. However, the strengths we do have for A directly address those very concerns.\u202fA\u2019s ability to **anticipate dangerous situations** and **see complex connections** demonstrates proactive risk assessment and the capacity to stay ahead of emerging threats\u2014behaviour that is essentially stress\u2011resilient. Moreover, A\u2019s **very good leadership qualities** imply an ability to guide and coordinate the cockpit crew effectively, which mitigates the lack of explicit crew\u2011cooperation notes.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fC, while showing **correct decisions quickly** and **calmness in a crisis**, also has documented **difficulty communicating ideas**, is **regarded as egocentric**, and is **not very willing to further his education**\u2014all red flags for sustained crew collaboration on long\u2011distance flights. Given that A\u2019s technical and leadership attributes already cover the critical safety dimensions, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fA is the best overall fit."}
